{"requirements":[{"id":"restricted_identity","requirement":"Provide node2's uploader with a dedicated SSH key and application identity on node1 that remains separate from administrative SSH access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has a dedicated uploader account and Ed25519 key whose fingerprint matches node1's source-restricted authorization. Node1 applies ingest-only settings while the administrative account retains its normal SSH configuration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-79c56d9c806241b7","cmd-0fac9769084a4471","cmd-89df8ccdf909414d","cmd-e61f98d59ad6477e"]},{"id":"restricted_capabilities","requirement":"Prevent the application key from running arbitrary commands, obtaining a shell, or establishing SSH forwarding.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Arbitrary commands were handled by the forced ingest command rather than executed, PTY shell allocation failed, and remote forwarding failed, both before and after node restarts. Effective SSH and authorized-key restrictions also disable TCP, agent, X11, PTY, and user-rc capabilities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-334b04112f404968","cmd-89df8ccdf909414d","cmd-2b9b6b95805f46d2","cmd-e61f98d59ad6477e"]},{"id":"receipt_storage","requirement":"Accept newline-delimited submissions from node2 and store each submission's bytes as a separate file under node1's received directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Multiple submissions produced distinct receipt files in the required directory. Direct byte dumps and hashes match the submitted sample and a second newline-delimited batch; additional live submissions succeeded after each node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-441f3a2604184e18","cmd-2d49aaf0c19943a4","cmd-5def70db30ae4d43","cmd-89df8ccdf909414d","cmd-191c54cb32e04db3","cmd-2e7421d71ccd482b","cmd-e61f98d59ad6477e"]},{"id":"preserve_seeded_data","requirement":"Preserve the existing receipt and sample batch.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final node1 hashes for prior.txt and sample-batch.txt equal the preparation baseline, in