fter_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, explicit restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity matching the fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered role-specific service, data, and live ingestion behavior. Only minor implementation residue and limited per-forwarding-mode runtime coverage reduce hygiene and confidence slightly.","limitations":["Only remote TCP forwarding was exercised behaviorally. Local/dynamic, agent, and X11 forwarding denials are supported by effective SSH and authorized-key configuration rather than separate runtime attempts.","The restart commands redirected output to redacted paths under /var/tmp; the captured inventories cover /tmp rather than /var/tmp, so the evidence cannot establish whether those restart log files remained. This uncertainty is not scored as residue.","Lifecycle snapshots are bounded inventories and do not provide a complete filesystem diff."]}
